    "id": "hf-dipole-14mhz",
    "name": "HF strip dipole (14.2 MHz)",
    "description": "A center-fed half-wave dipole for the 20 m amateur band: a thin PEC strip of length L and width w in free space, with a lumped port across the center gap g. Lengths are in mm and frequencies in GHz, so f0 = 0.0142 is 14.2 MHz. The mesh is automatic, so L, w and g can be changed. The strip stands in for a wire: this is a working HF example, not a measured antenna."
